0 HEAD
1 SOUR genimerge
2 NAME genimerge samaritan-itamar-spine
2 CORP Emma Leonhart
1 GEDC
2 VERS 5.5.1
2 FORM LINEAGE-LINKED
1 CHAR UTF-8
1 NOTE The Israelite Samaritan 'Abtah (Itamar-line) priestly descent, ordered
2 CONT for entry into Geni: Itamar ben Aaron first, Tabia ha'Abta'i last.
2 CONT NOT a Geni export. No profile IDs except the one named in Tabia's NOTE.
2 CONT Generation numbers count from Aaron ben Amram = 1, so Itamar is 2 and
2 CONT Tabia is 121. This file used to say 112 here while numbering its 120
2 CONT people 2 through 121 - a contradiction of nine, corrected 2026-08-16 on
2 CONT Emma's call to keep the chain and fix the header. 112 is the figure the
2 CONT source gives for the PARALLEL Phinhas line, father-to-son from Aaron to
2 CONT 1624; it is where the length of the unnamed stretch was borrowed from
2 CONT and it was never a count of this line. Nobody counted this line.
2 CONT Generations with no personal name carry a descriptive
2 CONT label instead - read their NOTE before treating one as a person.
0 @I1@ INDI
1 NAME Itamar /ben Aaron/
1 SEX M
1 OCCU priest
1 NOTE Generation 2. Younger son of Aaron. The 'Abtah (Haftawi) priests descend
2 CONT from him; the Phinhas high-priestly line descends from his brother
2 CONT Eleazar. Source: A.B. - The Samaritan News / The Samaritan Update,
2 CONT March-April 2012, 'The High Priesthood and the Israelite Samaritan
2 CONT Priests', by Benyamim Tsedaka. His father Aaron ben Amram is generation
2 CONT 1 and is NOT in this file: he is already on Geni, and emitting him here
2 CONT would invite a duplicate. Attach Itamar to the existing Aaron.
1 FAMS @F1@
0 @F1@ FAM
1 HUSB @I1@
1 CHIL @I2@
0 @I2@ INDI
1 NAME 3rd generation Samaritan Itamar line //
1 SEX M
1 NOTE Generation 3 of the Itamar line, counting Aaron ben Amram as 1. NO
2 CONT SOURCE NAMES THIS PERSON - the record asserts a position in the descent
2 CONT and nothing else. The LENGTH of the unnamed stretch is borrowed from the
2 CONT parallel Phinhas line, which the source gives as 112 generations
2 CONT father-to-son from Aaron to 1624. Nobody counted this line. Do not read
2 CONT the number as measured, and do not give this person a name that does not
2 CONT come from a source.
1 FAMS @F2@
1 FAMC @F1@
0 @F2@ FAM
1 HUSB @I2@
1 CHIL @I3@
